  {"squelch", "decay", "How long the filter takes to close again, in ms to fall 60 dB. An accented note always uses a short one."},
  {"squelch", "accent", "How much an accented note adds: more level, a sharper front and a wider filter sweep. Several accents in a row build on each other."},
  {"squelch", "slide", "How long a slide takes to reach the new note, in ms."},
  {"squelch", "drive", "Saturates the output."},
